## Tokens

Design tokens — colours, spacing, radii, sizing, motion durations and curves — are the vocabulary
everything else is written in. **No raw value belongs in consuming code** where a token exists.

Choose one of two shapes and delete the other:

### Shape A — tokens live in this project

If this project has a dedicated `tokens` document, that document owns the scales and this section is
one line pointing at it. Fill the list below in only if there is no such document.

Document each category with its token names and values, so a reviewer can check a literal against
the scale without reading code. `/audit-tokens` needs the *names*; a reader needs the values.

- **Colour System** — <!-- DERIVED: extract from the theme source named in profile.json's
     tokens.source. Group by role (brand / semantic / state / accent) rather than by hue: a
     reviewer needs to know which token *means* "error", not which one is red. -->
- **Typography** — named styles and their sizes. Note the minimum size and why.
- **Spacing** — the scale and its base unit. State whether off-scale values are ever allowed.
- **Border Radius** — the named radii and what each is for.
- **Sizing** — control heights and the minimum interactive target.
- **Motion** — durations and curves, or a cross-link if a separate motion document owns them.

### Shape B — tokens are owned elsewhere

Link out and **do not restate them here**. Two copies of a token table become two different token
tables, and the copy in the consuming project is always the stale one.

> Tokens and component specs live in <!-- DECIDE: the owning repository or package, by name and
> URL -->.
> Change them there and regenerate; never edit generated token output in this project.

State the accessor here anyway — the name consuming code uses to reach a token — because that is
what reviewers grep for and what `/audit-tokens` flags the absence of.

